{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02791",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.71,
      "end_seconds": 3.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Sorry, doctor, shall I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.67,
      "end_seconds": 10.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.03,
      "end_seconds": 24.24,
      "duration_seconds": 12.21,
      "text": "I've been feeling lightheaded during an episode, and I wanted to get it checked. I've been reading about it online and and it worried me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.86,
      "end_seconds": 28.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.0,
      "end_seconds": 33.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "it's been two weeks, I'm fairly sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.57,
      "end_seconds": 50.32,
      "duration_seconds": 14.75,
      "text": "tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse bear with me, I'm just building up the picture"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.68,
      "end_seconds": 66.23,
      "duration_seconds": 14.55,
      "text": "It, It sort of comes and goes. A seven out of ten, I suppose. Oh, and it stopping just as suddenly. That's been about the same, about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.25,
      "end_seconds": 71.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.43,
      "end_seconds": 86.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.04,
      "end_seconds": 109.36,
      "duration_seconds": 11.32,
      "text": "okay: respiratory rate 14, temp 36.4 degrees, heart rate 73, BP is 125 over 68, SpO2 97 percent on room air"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.46,
      "end_seconds": 113.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.13,
      "end_seconds": 118.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.97,
      "end_seconds": 123.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Let's move on to to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.44,
      "end_seconds": 133.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.41,
      "end_seconds": 138.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "take a deep breath for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.96,
      "end_seconds": 159.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "your heart sounds and rhythm are normal today"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.94,
      "end_seconds": 172.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Any family history of sudden death, breathlessness, fainting or chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.26,
      "end_seconds": 180.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "no, no family history of sudden death, breathlessness, fainting or chest pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.02,
      "end_seconds": 185.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.64,
      "end_seconds": 188.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.46,
      "end_seconds": 194.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Okay, do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.53,
      "end_seconds": 199.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.64,
      "end_seconds": 202.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.11,
      "end_seconds": 207.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.79,
      "end_seconds": 213.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Understood. A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.74,
      "end_seconds": 226.3,
      "duration_seconds": 11.56,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I walk the dog every morning. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.21,
      "end_seconds": 246.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Any regular medication at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.56,
      "end_seconds": 251.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No, I'm not on anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.23,
      "end_seconds": 266.42,
      "duration_seconds": 10.19,
      "text": "putting it all together, I don't have a clear answer today: episodes of supraventricular tachycardia is possible, and so is atrial fibrillation"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.67,
      "end_seconds": 292.09,
      "duration_seconds": 14.42,
      "text": "Try blowing hard against a closed mouth and nose when it starts. If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.78,
      "end_seconds": 298.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.86,
      "end_seconds": 301.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "have a good day"
    }
  ]
